# Testing rules

Run focused tests before broad suites.

For every repaired defect: add a focused unit test; add an integration test when behavior crosses subsystem boundaries; add a regression fixture when parsing or compatibility is involved; add failure-path coverage; add deterministic-output coverage; add byte-preservation coverage when incumbent files are involved.

Run at minimum:

- `gofmt` on changed Go files;
- `CGO_ENABLED=0 go test ./... -count=1`;
- `CGO_ENABLED=0 go vet ./...`;
- `CGO_ENABLED=0 go build ./cmd/m`;
- `CGO_ENABLED=0 go build ./cmd/mx`;
- `golangci-lint run ./...`;
- `govulncheck ./...`;
- `go run ./tools/check-license`;
- `go run ./tools/check-deps`;
- fixture verification;
- crash-shard verification;
- crash-tag integration tests;
- required pnpm conformance;
- unsupported-version tests;
- Nub fixture validation.

Run race separately: `go test -race ./... -count=1`.

Do not report: skipped tests as passed; unavailable commands as passed; partial suites as full suites; flaky failures as success; deferred functionality as complete; parse-only tests as mutation conformance.
